{
  "name": "incident-response",
  "description": "Run a production incident end to end: declare and classify severity, assign command roles, capture the timeline, post customer updates, triage metrics and changes, stabilize first by rollback, flag, scale or traffic shift, correlate logs and traces, test hypotheses with stack-specific runtime and database evidence, verify the fix, resolve, and run a blameless postmortem with tracked follow-ups. Set user inputs stack (python, node, go, java), database (postgres, mysql), log_backend (loki, cloudwatch) and trace_backend (tempo) to route conditional steps.",
